---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const CONTACT = 'benjamindavisma@gmail.com';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Benjamin Davis"
  description="What benjamindavis.build does and does not collect. No cookies, no analytics, no tracking."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="11 November 2026"
>

  <p>
    This site is a personal portfolio run by Benjamin Davis. It is deliberately
    built to collect as close to nothing as a website can. There are no
    accounts, no cookies set by this site, no analytics, and no advertising or
    tracking scripts of any kind.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects</h2>

  <p>
    Nothing. The site is a set of static pages. It has no database, no login,
    and no server-side code that receives anything you type.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact and order forms</h2>

  <p>
    The forms on the <a href="/contact">contact</a> and card-order pages do not
    submit anything to this site. When you press send, the form assembles what
    you typed into a message and hands it to whatever email program your device
    uses. Nothing leaves your device until you send that email yourself, from
    your own address, and you can edit or discard it first.
  </p>

  <p>
    Once you do send it, the message sits in an ordinary Gmail inbox, subject to
    Google's own privacy terms. It is used to reply to you and nothing else — it
    is never sold, shared, or added to a mailing list.
  </p>

  <h2>What other companies see</h2>

  <p>
    Serving a page at all means some third parties necessarily see a request
    from you. Specifically:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Fonts.</strong> Typefaces are loaded from
      <span>fonts.googleapis.com</span> and <span>fonts.gstatic.com</span>, so
      Google receives your IP address and browser user-agent when a page loads.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Vercel.</strong> The site is hosted on Vercel, which keeps
      standard server logs of requests, including IP addresses.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare.</strong> Cloudflare sits in front of the site for DNS,
      caching, and bot protection. It inspects requests and may set its own
      security cookies to tell real visitors from automated traffic.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    None of these are chosen to gather information about you, and none of their
    data is accessible to or used by this site beyond the fact that pages get
    served.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>

  <p>
    Pages here link out to places like LinkedIn and fair or award organisations.
    Once you follow a link you are on someone else's site under someone else's
    privacy policy, and this one no longer applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13 and knowingly collects no
    information from anyone, children included.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <p>
    Because nothing is collected, there is generally nothing to request, correct,
    or delete. The exception is an email you chose to send: write to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> and it will be deleted on
    request.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.
    There is no archive of previous versions — the current text is the whole
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about this policy can go to
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
